import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,an as d}from"./chunks/framework.Y04DxkVZ.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"For NicheMapR users","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"manual/nichemapr.md","filePath":"manual/nichemapr.md","lastUpdated":null}'),r={name:"manual/nichemapr.md"};function c(n,e,i,l,s,h){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[d('<h1 id="For-NicheMapR-users" tabindex="-1">For NicheMapR users <a class="header-anchor" href="#For-NicheMapR-users" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;For NicheMapR users {#For-NicheMapR-users}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>HeatExchange.jl descends from the heat budget code of <a href="https://github.com/mrke/NicheMapR" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NicheMapR</a>: the ectotherm model (Kearney and Porter 2020), the endotherm model (Kearney et al. 2021) and its human extension, HomoTherm (Kearney et al. 2026). The physics is the same. The structure is not, and this page explains what moved where.</p><h2 id="Two-programs-become-one-question-with-two-answers" tabindex="-1">Two programs become one question with two answers <a class="header-anchor" href="#Two-programs-become-one-question-with-two-answers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Two programs become one question with two answers {#Two-programs-become-one-question-with-two-answers}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>NicheMapR is organised by kind of organism. The ectotherm model finds the body temperature at which the heat budget balances, for an animal with bare skin whose metabolic heat is small. The endotherm model does the reverse: it holds the core temperature at a set value and finds the metabolic rate that balances the budget, for an animal that may have fur and fat. Each has its own Fortran library, with its own routines for geometry, solar radiation, convection and evaporation, and its own R interface.</p><p>Kearney et al. (2021) noted that this split reflects a real biological difference, the far greater energetic intensity of endotherms, but the split is not a physical one. Both programs solve the same steady-state heat budget. They differ in two things only:</p><ul><li><p><strong>which quantity is unknown</strong>: the core temperature, or the rate of metabolic heat production, and</p></li><li><p><strong>what the surface is</strong>: bare skin, or skin under a layer of fur or feathers.</p></li></ul><p>HeatExchange.jl is organised by those two things, and any combination of them can be solved:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;"></th><th style="text-align:left;">Bare skin</th><th style="text-align:left;">Insulated</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Solve for temperature</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">the NicheMapR ectotherm model, and leaves</td><td style="text-align:left;"><em>new</em>: a torpid or dead endotherm, a furred insect, a chick before it can thermoregulate</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Solve for metabolic rate</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><em>new</em>: a naked endotherm, a thermogenic flower</td><td style="text-align:left;">the NicheMapR endotherm model</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The first row is <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_temperature"><code>solve_temperature</code></a> and the second is <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_metabolic_rate</code></a>. Which column applies is decided by the body: a <code>Body</code> with <code>Naked()</code> insulation takes the bare-skin path and one with a fibrous layer takes the insulated path, see <a href="./solvers">Temperature or metabolic rate</a>. The heat-flow functions underneath are shared, so there is one <code>convection</code>, one <code>evaporation</code> and one <code>respiration</code> where NicheMapR has two of each.</p><h2 id="What-moved-where" tabindex="-1">What moved where <a class="header-anchor" href="#What-moved-where" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What moved where {#What-moved-where}&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">NicheMapR</th><th style="text-align:left;">Here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ectotherm</code> / <code>ectoR_devel</code>: <code>FUN</code> solved for <code>TC</code> by <code>ZBRENT</code> (<code>uniroot</code> in R)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.heat_balance"><code>heat_balance</code></a> solved by <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_temperature"><code>solve_temperature</code></a> with <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.zbrent"><code>zbrent</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>SOLAR</code>, <code>RADIN</code>, <code>RADOUT</code>, <code>CONV</code>, <code>COND</code>, <code>SEVAP</code>, <code>RESP</code>, <code>MET</code> and their <code>_ecto</code> and <code>_ENDO</code> versions</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solar"><code>solar</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.radiation_in"><code>radiation_in</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.radiation_out"><code>radiation_out</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.convection"><code>convection</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.conduction"><code>conduction</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.evaporation"><code>evaporation</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.respiration"><code>respiration</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.metabolic_rate"><code>metabolic_rate</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>endoR</code> / <code>endoR_devel</code> / <code>SOLVENDO</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_metabolic_rate</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>IRPROP</code>, <code>GETKFUR</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.insulation_properties"><code>insulation_properties</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.insulation_thermal_conductivity"><code>insulation_thermal_conductivity</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>SIMULSOL</code>, called for the dorsal and the ventral side</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_temperatures"><code>solve_temperatures</code></a> for each side, on the residuals of <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_part_heat_balance"><code>solve_part_heat_balance</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ZBRENT_ENDO</code> on <code>RESPFUN</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.zbrent"><code>zbrent</code></a> on the <code>balance</code> returned by <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.respiration"><code>respiration</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">the closed-form flesh, fat and fur conduction of each shape</td><td style="text-align:left;">a stack of radial layers, see <a href="./radial_layers">Layers as a radial graph</a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">the allometric metabolic rate equations in <code>MET</code> and <code>QBASAL</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.MetabolicRateEquation"><code>MetabolicRateEquation</code></a> types here for now, moving to <a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/BiologicalScaling.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BiologicalScaling.jl</a>, see <a href="./metabolism">Metabolism</a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ellipsoid_endo</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.ellipsoid_endotherm"><code>ellipsoid_endotherm</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>leaf = 1</code> in <code>ectotherm</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.LeafEvaporationParameters"><code>LeafEvaporationParameters</code></a> in place of <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.AnimalEvaporationParameters"><code>AnimalEvaporationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>HomoTherm</code>: <code>endoR</code> once per body part, summed</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_coupled_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_coupled_metabolic_rate</code></a> over the parts of a body, see <a href="./multipart">Bodies of many parts</a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>GEOM</code>, <code>GEOM_ENDO</code>, the geometric shape codes</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/BiophysicalGeometry.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BiophysicalGeometry.jl</a>: <code>Cylinder</code>, <code>Sphere</code>, <code>Plate</code>, <code>Ellipsoid</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">the empirical surface areas in <code>GEOM</code> and <code>GEOM_ENDO</code>: the desert iguana and leopard frog, and the bird and mammal options of <code>SAMODE</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/BiologicalScaling.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BiologicalScaling.jl</a>, which already has the bird and mammal surface areas (<code>surface_area(EutherianMammal(), mass)</code>). These are allometric relations, not geometry. <code>DesertIguana</code> and <code>LeopardFrog</code> are still in BiophysicalGeometry.jl in this version, and are to be removed from it in favour of BiologicalScaling.jl</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>DRYAIR</code>, <code>WETAIR</code>, <code>VAPPRS</code>, <code>WATER</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/FluidProperties.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FluidProperties.jl</a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">the thermoregulation loops of <code>ectotherm</code> (shade, posture, burrow, climb) and of <code>endoR</code> (uncurl, vasodilate, raise core temperature, pant, sweat)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/BiophysicalBehaviour.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BiophysicalBehaviour.jl</a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">transient heat budgets: <code>onelump</code>, <code>onelump_var</code>, <code>twolump</code>, <code>trans_behav</code>, and the transient option of <code>ectotherm</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">to be added to this package: the residual of <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.heat_balance"><code>heat_balance</code></a> tracked through time, in a varying environment, and turned into body temperature by the heat capacity. <code>trans_behav</code> and the behaviour of the transient <code>ectotherm</code> are for BiophysicalBehaviour.jl</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;">the Dynamic Energy Budget model of <code>ectotherm</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">not in this package</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>micro_global</code> and the other microclimate functions</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/Microclimate.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Microclimate.jl</a> and <a href="https://github.com/BiophysicalEcology/SolarRadiation.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SolarRadiation.jl</a></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The last four rows are the largest change in scope. <code>ectotherm</code> is a whole simulation: it reads a year of microclimate, chooses where the animal is each hour, and can run an energy budget alongside. <code>endoR</code> includes a thermoregulatory sequence. This package does neither. It takes one organism in one environment and solves its heat budget, and it is the layer that the behaviour and life-cycle packages call. It corresponds most closely to <code>ectoR_devel</code>, and to <code>endoR_devel</code> with <code>THERMOREG = 0</code>.</p><h2 id="There-is-no-separate-transient-program" tabindex="-1">There is no separate transient program <a class="header-anchor" href="#There-is-no-separate-transient-program" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;There is no separate transient program {#There-is-no-separate-transient-program}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transient functions of NicheMapR are separate analytical or numerical solutions for a lump of tissue with heat storage, written apart from the steady-state code. Here a transient calculation needs no new physics. <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.heat_balance"><code>heat_balance</code></a> returns the net heat flow of an organism at a given temperature, which is the rate of heat storage. A steady state is where that is zero. A transient is its integral through time, divided by the heat capacity. The transient calculation of this package is to be exactly that: the residuals of the code described here, tracked through time in an environment that may vary, as in <code>onelump_var</code>, with no second set of equations. It is not yet in the version that this documentation describes.</p><h2 id="Dorsal-and-ventral" tabindex="-1">Dorsal and ventral <a class="header-anchor" href="#Dorsal-and-ventral" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dorsal and ventral {#Dorsal-and-ventral}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The fur and the surroundings of an animal differ between its back and its belly. <code>endoR</code> deals with this by calling <code>SIMULSOL</code> twice, once for a whole animal covered in dorsal fur and facing the sky, and once for a whole animal covered in ventral fur and facing the ground, and taking a weighted mean of the two heat flows. This is kept, as the <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.MultiSided"><code>MultiSided</code></a> strategy, and it reproduces <code>endoR</code>.</p><p>It is also now a special case. A body can be two real halves joined at a shared core, each with its own coat, area and view, exchanging heat with each other. The tutorial <a href="./../tutorials/two_parts">Back and belly: two halves</a> compares the two.</p><h2 id="Layers" tabindex="-1">Layers <a class="header-anchor" href="#Layers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Layers {#Layers}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>endoR</code> has one layer of flesh, an optional layer of fat set by <code>FATPCT</code>, and one layer of fur, and the heat flow through them is written out for each shape. Here the core-to-skin conduction is an ordered list of layers, each with a resistance that depends on its shape, added in series. One flesh layer and one fat layer reproduce <code>endoR</code> to machine precision. See <a href="./radial_layers">Layers as a radial graph</a> for what this makes possible.</p><h2 id="Many-parts" tabindex="-1">Many parts <a class="header-anchor" href="#Many-parts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Many parts {#Many-parts}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>HomoTherm</code> showed how to build an animal from several parts: run the endotherm model for each part without respiration, add up the heat that each part must be supplied with, and close the respiration balance once for the whole animal. Each part gives up a fixed fraction of its area, <code>PJOINs</code>, to its joins with the others. That scheme is <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_coupled_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_coupled_metabolic_rate</code></a>. The parts are those of a <code>CompositeBody</code>, so the hidden areas and the view that each part has of the sky, the ground and the other parts come from where the parts are. Parts can also hold different core temperatures and conduct heat to each other, which <code>HomoTherm</code> does not do. The tutorial <a href="./../tutorials/human">A human of many parts</a> rebuilds the <code>HomoTherm</code> human.</p><p>The body itself is built with BiophysicalGeometry.jl. Each part is a <code>Body</code>, a shape with its own layers, and the parts are joined at named surfaces into a <code>CompositeBody</code>, with a <code>Join</code> for each connection that says where on each part the join is and how large it is. The package then gives the area that each join hides, each part&#39;s silhouette with the shade of the other parts on it, and each part&#39;s view of the sky, the ground and the other parts, which are the inputs that the heat budget of a part needs. Its documentation has tutorials that build a dog, a cow and this human, and an interactive page, <a href="https://biophysicalecology.github.io/BiophysicalGeometry.jl/dev/builder" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Build an animal</a>, on which an animal is assembled with sliders and the code that builds it can be copied.</p><h2 id="Parameter-names" tabindex="-1">Parameter names <a class="header-anchor" href="#Parameter-names" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Parameter names {#Parameter-names}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The parameters are grouped into structs by process, with names in words, see <a href="./parameters">Parameters</a>.</p><h3 id="Ectotherm" tabindex="-1">Ectotherm <a class="header-anchor" href="#Ectotherm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Ectotherm {#Ectotherm}&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;"><code>ectoR_devel</code></th><th style="text-align:left;">Here</th><th style="text-align:left;">In</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>Ww_g</code>, <code>rho_body</code>, <code>shape</code>, <code>shape_b</code>, <code>shape_c</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">mass, density, shape type and axis ratios</td><td style="text-align:left;">the shape, from BiophysicalGeometry.jl</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>alpha</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>body_absorptivity_dorsal</code>, <code>body_absorptivity_ventral</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>epsilon</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>body_emissivity_dorsal</code>, <code>body_emissivity_ventral</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>fatosk</code>, <code>fatosb</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>sky_view_factor</code>, <code>ground_view_factor</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>postur</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>solar_orientation</code>: <code>Intermediate()</code>, <code>NormalToSun()</code>, <code>ParallelToSun()</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>pct_cond</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>conduction_fraction</code> (0 to 1)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.ExternalConductionParameters"><code>ExternalConductionParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>k_flesh</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>flesh_conductivity</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.InternalConductionParameters"><code>InternalConductionParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>pct_wet</code>, <code>pct_eyes</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>skin_wetness</code>, <code>eye_fraction</code> (0 to 1)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.AnimalEvaporationParameters"><code>AnimalEvaporationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>pct_mouth</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>mouth_fraction</code> (0 to 1)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RespirationParameters"><code>RespirationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>psi_body</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>water_potential</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.HydraulicParameters"><code>HydraulicParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>F_O2</code> (%), <code>RQ</code>, <code>pantmax</code>, <code>delta_air</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>oxygen_extraction_efficiency</code>, <code>respiratory_quotient</code>, <code>pant</code>, <code>exhaled_temperature_offset</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RespirationParameters"><code>RespirationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>M_1</code>, <code>M_2</code>, <code>M_3</code>, <code>M_4</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>mass_normalisation</code>, <code>mass_exponent</code>, <code>thermal_sensitivity</code>, <code>metabolic_state</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.AndrewsPough2"><code>AndrewsPough2</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>g_vs_ab</code>, <code>g_vs_ad</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>abaxial_vapour_conductance</code>, <code>adaxial_vapour_conductance</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.LeafEvaporationParameters"><code>LeafEvaporationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>1 - alpha_sub</code>, <code>epsilon_sub</code>, <code>epsilon_sky</code>, <code>elev</code>, <code>fluid</code>, <code>conv_enhance</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ground_albedo</code>, <code>ground_emissivity</code>, <code>sky_emissivity</code>, <code>elevation</code>, <code>fluid</code>, <code>convection_enhancement</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalPars"><code>EnvironmentalPars</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>O2gas</code>, <code>CO2gas</code>, <code>N2gas</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>GasFractions(oxygen, carbon_dioxide, nitrogen)</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalPars"><code>EnvironmentalPars</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>TA</code>, <code>TSKY</code>, <code>TGRD</code>, <code>TSUBST</code>, <code>VEL</code>, <code>RH</code> (%), <code>pres</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>air_temperature</code>, <code>sky_temperature</code>, <code>ground_temperature</code>, <code>substrate_temperature</code>, <code>wind_speed</code>, <code>relative_humidity</code> (0 to 1), <code>atmospheric_pressure</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalVars"><code>EnvironmentalVars</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>QSOLR</code>, <code>Z</code>, <code>PDIF</code>, <code>SHADE</code> (%), <code>K_sub</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>global_radiation</code>, <code>zenith_angle</code>, <code>diffuse_fraction</code>, <code>shade</code> (0 to 1), <code>substrate_conductivity</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalVars"><code>EnvironmentalVars</code></a></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="Endotherm" tabindex="-1">Endotherm <a class="header-anchor" href="#Endotherm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Endotherm {#Endotherm}&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;"><code>endoR_devel</code></th><th style="text-align:left;">Here</th><th style="text-align:left;">In</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>AMASS</code>, <code>ANDENS</code>, <code>SHAPE</code>, <code>SHAPE_B</code>, <code>SHAPE_C</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">mass, density, shape type and axis ratios</td><td style="text-align:left;">the shape</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>FATPCT</code> (%), <code>FATDEN</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>FatLayer(fraction, density)</code>; <code>fat_fraction</code>, <code>fat_density</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">the body; <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.InternalConductionParameters"><code>InternalConductionParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>AK1</code>, <code>AK2</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>flesh_conductivity</code>, <code>fat_conductivity</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.InternalConductionParameters"><code>InternalConductionParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>DHAIRD</code>, <code>LHAIRD</code>, <code>ZFURD</code>, <code>RHOD</code>, <code>REFLD</code>, <code>KHAIR</code> (and <code>…V</code>)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>diameter</code>, <code>length</code>, <code>depth</code>, <code>density</code>, <code>reflectance</code>, <code>conductivity</code> of <code>dorsal</code> (and <code>ventral</code>)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.FibreProperties"><code>FibreProperties</code></a> in <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.InsulationParameters"><code>InsulationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ZFURCOMP</code>, <code>XR</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>depth_compressed</code>, <code>longwave_depth_fraction</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.InsulationParameters"><code>InsulationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>PVEN</code>, <code>PCOND</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ventral_fraction</code>, <code>conduction_fraction</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a>, <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.ExternalConductionParameters"><code>ExternalConductionParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>EMISAN</code>, <code>FSKREF</code>, <code>FGDREF</code>, <code>FABUSH</code>, <code>ORIENT</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>body_emissivity_…</code>, <code>sky_view_factor</code>, <code>ground_view_factor</code>, <code>bush_view_factor</code>, <code>solar_orientation</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>1 - REFLD</code>, <code>1 - REFLV</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>body_absorptivity_dorsal</code>, <code>body_absorptivity_ventral</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RadiationParameters"><code>RadiationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>PCTWET</code>, <code>FURWET</code>, <code>PCTEYES</code>, <code>PCTBAREVAP</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>skin_wetness</code>, <code>insulation_wetness</code>, <code>eye_fraction</code>, <code>bare_skin_fraction</code> (0 to 1)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.AnimalEvaporationParameters"><code>AnimalEvaporationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>EXTREF</code> (%), <code>RQ</code>, <code>PANT</code>, <code>DELTAR</code>, <code>RELXIT</code> (%)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>oxygen_extraction_efficiency</code>, <code>respiratory_quotient</code>, <code>pant</code>, <code>exhaled_temperature_offset</code>, <code>exhaled_relative_humidity</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.RespirationParameters"><code>RespirationParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>TC</code>, <code>QBASAL</code>, <code>Q10</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>core_temperature</code>, <code>metabolic_heat_flow</code>, <code>q10</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.MetabolismParameters"><code>MetabolismParameters</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>RESPIRE</code>, <code>DIFTOL</code>, <code>BRENTOL</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>respire</code>, <code>temperature_error_tolerance</code>, <code>resp_tolerance</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.SolveMetabolicRateOptions"><code>SolveMetabolicRateOptions</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>TS</code>, <code>TFA</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">the starting <code>skin_temperature</code> and <code>insulation_temperature</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">arguments of <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_metabolic_rate</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>1 - ABSSB</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>ground_albedo</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalPars"><code>EnvironmentalPars</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>TAREF</code>, <code>TBUSH</code>, <code>TCONDSB</code>, <code>KSUB</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>reference_air_temperature</code>, <code>bush_temperature</code>, <code>substrate_temperature</code>, <code>substrate_conductivity</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.EnvironmentalVars"><code>EnvironmentalVars</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>UNCURL</code>, <code>SHAPE_B_MAX</code>, <code>AK1_INC</code>, <code>AK1_MAX</code>, <code>TC_INC</code>, <code>TC_MAX</code>, <code>PANT_INC</code>, <code>PANT_MAX</code>, <code>PCTWET_INC</code>, <code>PCTWET_MAX</code>, <code>TREGMODE</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">limits and steps of thermoregulation</td><td style="text-align:left;">BiophysicalBehaviour.jl</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Percentages in NicheMapR are fractions here, and temperatures in °C are <a href="https://github.com/PainterQubits/Unitful.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Unitful.jl</a> quantities in any unit of temperature.</p><h3 id="Outputs" tabindex="-1">Outputs <a class="header-anchor" href="#Outputs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Outputs {#Outputs}&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">NicheMapR table</th><th style="text-align:left;">Here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>enbal</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>energy_balance</code> from <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_temperature"><code>solve_temperature</code></a>; <code>energy_flows</code> from <a href="/HeatExchange.jl/previews/PR57/api#HeatExchange.solve_metabolic_rate"><code>solve_metabolic_rate</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>treg</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>thermoregulation</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>masbal</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>mass_balance</code>; <code>mass_flows</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>morph</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>morphology</code>, and the body itself</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="How-closely-the-numbers-agree" tabindex="-1">How closely the numbers agree <a class="header-anchor" href="#How-closely-the-numbers-agree" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How closely the numbers agree {#How-closely-the-numbers-agree}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The tests of the package compare it with output saved from NicheMapR, and the tutorials show the comparisons.</p><p>For a bare-skinned ectotherm the body temperature and every heat and mass flow agree with <code>ectoR_devel</code> to within one part in ten thousand, and the geometry to within rounding.</p><p>For an endotherm, the geometry agrees with <code>endoR_devel</code> to within rounding and the core and lung temperatures to within 0.1 %. The skin and fur temperatures, the fur conductivity and the surface heat flows agree to within about 0.3 %, and the metabolic rate to within about 1 %. The difference has a known cause. <code>SIMULSOL</code> updates the fur surface temperature with a linearised form of the surface heat balance and stops when successive guesses agree within <code>DIFTOL</code>. Here the two surface temperatures are found by a Newton iteration that balances the surface energy budget to within 10⁻⁹. The metabolic rate depends on the small difference between the core and skin temperatures, so a small change in skin temperature is a larger relative change in metabolic rate.</p>',35)])])}const f=t(r,[["render",c]]);export{g as __pageData,f as default};
